  "executive_briefing": "As the U.S. Senate prepares for a pivotal vote on the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633) on September 15, 2026, the digital asset market is undergoing structural realignment. The legislation provides regulatory boundaries between the SEC and CFTC, enabling institutions and developers to deploy native programmability, smart contracts, and secure vaults directly on Bitcoin. This technological shift poses direct competition to Ethereum's smart contract monopoly. Concurrently, institutional Bitcoin allocation has transitioned from early ETF accumulation into mature treasury management, while cross-chain DeFi adopts trust-minimized asset swaps to safely connect isolated liquidity pools.",
